<body>
    <h1>Access Control to the Display in IGEL OS 12</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>This article shows how to control access to the display in IGEL =
OS. Device access control<strong>&nbsp;</strong>is enabled by default.</p>
<hr>
<p>Menu path: <strong>User Interface &gt; Display Settings &gt; Access Cont=
rol</strong></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-=
wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-=
image confluence-content-image-border image-left" width=3D"468" loading=3D"=
lazy" src=3D"ebaf117632a7672cb3d110b98ee0a6da59f4914da9e9296476272893fc2a2b=
a5" data-image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachm=
ents/73302715/OS12_Display_Access%20Control.png?version=3D1&amp;modificatio=
nDate=3D1716364672282&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"837=
" data-width=3D"1280" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resou=
rce-id=3D"73308835" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource=
-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"OS12_Display_Acc=
ess Control.png" data-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" dat=
a-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container=
-id=3D"73302715" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"3" data-media-id=
=3D"8a6a6a2f-71c5-47d1-8f79-894243b4de14" data-media-type=3D"file" height=
=3D"306"></span>
<p><strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"5bd2318b-7885-=
4414-9958-1149ef3dedeb">Disable</span> console switching</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 You can NOT switch to the console using [Ctrl] + [Alt] + [F11]=
 or [Ctrl] + [Alt] + [F12].</p>
<p>=E2=98=90&nbsp;You can access the console using [Ctrl] + [Alt] + [F11] o=
r [Ctrl] + [Alt] + [F12]. (Default)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Access control</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 Access to this display from other computers will be controlled=
. (Default)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Disable TCP connections</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 All TCP connections to the display are disabled. Only local ap=
plications are displayed. The xhost mechanism does not function. (Default)<=
/p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>This parameter is ignored if XDMCP is configured.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<p><strong>List of Trusted X Hosts</strong></p>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"f051c014-743c-4e44-b57=
4-b663e212f9ac">List</span> of approved computers for console access</p>
<p>To manage the list:</p>
<div class=3D"error">
<span class=3D"error">Unable to render {include}</span> The included page c=
ould not be found.
</div>
<p>When adding the <strong>Trusted host</strong>, give the name of the remo=
te host (not the IP address) you would like to add.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
